{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIxL0hhbmRsZSUyMFdpdGglMjBDYXJlJTIwVGhlJTIwTGVnZW5kJTIwT2YlMjBUaGUlMjBOb3RpYyUyMFN0cmVldGJhbGwlMjBDcmV3JTIwJTI4MjAyMSUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Handle With Care The Legend Of The Notic Streetball Crew","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/keQ2rTKoNCS2fPSIHVBwQovXLTu.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/67QCaE1S2ZAV1GWtvS0b37FOB46.jpg","description":"Largely composed of immigrants and first-generation Canadians from Vancouver’s suburbs, The Notic underground basketball collective overcame all odds to achieve global fame 20 years ago. In defiance of their high school coaches’ casual racism and desire for oppressive conformity, this gregarious group discovered self-expression through streetball’s loose structure and aversion to rules. Bursting onto the scene at the NBA-sponsored Hoop It Up tournament near Science World, the group unleashed a devastating arsenal of bravura tricks and moves. DIY VHS highlights of their showstopping exploits would soon be collected on their first \"mixtape\". With copies finding their way to every corner of the globe, it was anointed \"the bible of streetball\".\n\nReleased 8 Oct 2021 · Canada, United States of America · Language: English · 86 min\nStudio: The Notic Studios Inc, TELUS originals, RTG Features\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2021","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"runtime":"86 min","cast":["Jermaine Foster","Rory Grace","Joey Haywood","Andrew Liew","David Mubanda","Jonathan Mubanda","Dauphin Ngongo","Jamal Parker"],"director":["Kirk Thomas","Jeremy Schaulin-Rioux"],"released":"2021-10-08T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Kirk Thomas","character":"Director"},{"name":"Jermaine Foster","character":"Self (Archival Footage)"},{"name":"Rory Grace","character":"Self (Archival Footage)"},{"name":"Joey Haywood","character":"Self (Archival Footage)"},{"name":"Andrew Liew